Package: bridgeoverlap
Type: Package
Title: Overlap Checks and Failure Diagnostics for Bridge Sampling
Version: 1.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Giorgio", "Micaletto", email = "gmicaletto@uchicago.edu",
           role = c("aut", "cre")))
Description: Diagnostics for the optimal bridge sampling estimator of
    Meng and Wong (1996), computed as the root of the score of an intercept-only
    logistic regression that separates posterior from proposal draws. From the
    fitted responsibilities the package computes, at no extra cost, the
    delta-method Monte Carlo standard error (MCSE) with a within-chain long-run
    variance, and two checks of it: the overlap check, based on the estimated
    effective overlap, and the variance check, a delete-a-group jackknife
    comparison. It also gives a finite-sample confidence interval, based on
    Bennett's inequality for independent draws and on a Bernstein inequality for
    reversible Markov chains with a known bound on the spectral gap, and a
    decision rule that maps each failed check to an action. Works on objects returned by
    'bridgesampling::bridge_sampler()' and provides helpers for 'cmdstanr' fits,
    including two-fold cross-fitting.
